/F1 18 Tf
(14.1 Simple Harmonic Motion) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
T*
T*
(When a mass is attached to an ideal spring, the spring exerts a restoring force.) Tj
T*
(Hooke's law states that the restoring force is proportional to displacement, F = -kx.) Tj
T*
(The resulting motion is called simple harmonic motion.) Tj
T*
(The angular frequency of the mass-spring system is omega = sqrt\(k/m\).) Tj
T*
(The period of oscillation is T = 2 pi sqrt\(m/k\) and does not depend on amplitude.) Tj
T*
(The amplitude is the maximum displacement from the equilibrium position.) Tj
T*
(Determine the angular frequency of a mass-spring system if k = 200 N/m.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
